# Playwright: host OS only

Playwright e2e **must** run on the real machine, not the Cursor command sandbox.

The harness starts `go run`, Vite, Chromium, and talks to Docker sample DBs on `127.0.0.1`. Sandbox (and `full_network` alone) blocks browser launch, port bind, and Docker.

## How to run

When using the Shell tool for any of:

- `cd e2e && npm test …`
- `npm run test:pg` / `test:mysql` / `test:sqlite` / `test:ui`
- `npx playwright install …`
- `docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml …` (sample DBs for e2e)
- `npx playwright show-trace …`

pass **`required_permissions: ["all"]`** on the **first** invocation. Do not try sandbox first and retry.

```
# ❌ BAD — default sandbox (or full_network only)
cd e2e && npm test -- tests/shared/harness-smoke.spec.ts

# ✅ GOOD — Shell tool with required_permissions: ["all"]
cd e2e && npm test -- tests/shared/harness-smoke.spec.ts
```

Still use `cd e2e && npm test` (via `run-e2e`). Never `npx playwright test` alone.
